<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Crescentia of Kaufbeuren</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1682–1744</span> · Also known as Maria Crescentia Höss</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Crescentia of Kaufbeuren, born Anna Höss, was a Franciscan nun in the convent of Kaufbeuren in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swabia-bavaria">Bavarian Swabia</a>, of which she became mother superior in 1741. Known for her mystical piety and sought out for advice by visitors of every rank, she was beatified in 1900 and canonised by Pope John Paul II in 2001.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/crescentia-of-kaufbeuren.jpg" alt="Crescentia of Kaufbeuren" width="143" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: DieAlraune · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Crescentiah%C3%B6ss.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
